# A slow boot (source/ezkernelnew.c, Boot_notice_check): LOGGING on and a
# card without a log, whose 64 KB file takes about 80 frames to make. The
# "Loading..." notice comes up 20 frames after the card mounted, fading in
# from black, then fades out before the SD list comes in, every frame of
# both fades hashed (v0.3.2: it cut in, after a frame of the background,
# and cut out). A fast boot shows none (golden boot).
#! settings 26=2
-w "boot: still busy 20 frames after mounting"
-H @0:@12
-w "screen ready: notice"
-s @1:notice.png
-w "boot: handing over"
-H @0:@6
-w "screen ready: sd-list"
-s @1:list.png
